  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">World Bank Group Governance &amp; Institutions Umbrella Programme (G&amp;I Multi-Donor Trust Fund)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The G&amp;I Programme supports client countries in improving their effectiveness and accountability e.g. public sector performance and strengthening institutional reform, leveraging the power of digital and technology solutions in the public sector, and enhancing transparency and accountability. Technical and financial support is provided on a wide range of thematic areas broadly focused on: accelerating global learning and institutional change by sharing good practices, generating new lessons, investing in global knowledge, and ensuring partners are well informed and guided on what is working and empowered to implement reforms.

The structure is around three broad modules: 
&#x2022;	Organisation and People which supports public administration and institutions reform, subnational governance and decentralisation.
&#x2022;	Open Government, Anticorruption, and Technology supporting openness and transparency and reducing corruption, including building upon the WB&#x2019;s new Anticorruption Action Plan and GovTech.
&#x2022;	Institutions of Accountability supporting justice and the rule of law, legislative bodies, multi-stakeholder engagement and citizen-centric reforms.</narrative>
  </description>
